From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zach Taylor <zctaylor.work@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 17:28:22 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 18/30] Match HTTPS egress rules on exact request paths

A path_prefixes entry must end with "/", so a rule could not allow one
exact path. HttpsRule.paths carries exact paths. A request whose path up
to "?" equals an entry matches, and an exact match beats any prefix.

CheckExactPath holds the one format rule that admission and Compile
share. Compile drops a bad entry without widening the rule. The tie check
keys an exact path apart from a prefix and from a rule with neither.

Fork-Topic: egress-paths
Fork-Upstream: candidate
